## Architecture

Evaluation Structures own their canonical payload, structure-specific
validation, normalization and draft/submit semantics.

Evaluation payloads are persisted using Mongoose `Schema.Types.Mixed`.
Do not change shared persistence schemas.

## Backend error contract

Use the existing factories from:

```text
Backend/utils/common/errors.js
```

Relevant APIs:

```js
createBadRequestError(message, { field, details });
createInternalError(message, { field, details });
```

Use `createBadRequestError` for invalid user-controlled/persisted evaluation
input: malformed payloads, invalid values, duplicate/unknown submitted IDs,
incomplete submit data, unsupported save modes, or malformed creator remapping
input.

Use `createInternalError` when application-provided runtime context is malformed
or inconsistent, such as invalid `decisionContext`, invalid canonical
collections, or duplicate/invalid canonical IDs supplied by the application.

Do not use plain `Error`/`TypeError` where these application errors apply.
Include `field` and useful `details` when possible.

## Shared Backend utilities

Existing APIs include:

```text
Backend/utils/common/objects.js
  isPlainObject(value)
  hasOwnKey(object, key)

Backend/utils/common/strings.js
  normalizeNonEmptyString(value)
  isNonEmptyString(value)
```

Prefer these when semantics match. Do not recreate equivalent generic helpers.

For the standard draft/submit required-value distinction:

```text
Backend/modules/decisionPlugins/evaluations/shared/resolveRequireValue.js
```

provides:

```js
resolveRequireValue(mode)
```

It returns false for `"draft"`, true for `"submit"` and already uses BAD_REQUEST
for unsupported modes. Use it only when that abstraction matches the structure.

## Public contract

GET:

```js
async ({ payload, decisionContext }) => frontendPayload
```

SAVE:

```js
async ({ payload, decisionContext, mode }) => storedPayload
```

`mode` is `"draft"` or `"submit"`.

Return complete payloads. Do not mutate input payload/context.

