## Implementation style

Use ES modules, shared helpers/errors, immutable inputs and deliberate
normalization. Keep structure-specific logic local. Put pure structure-specific
operations in `operations/` only when useful. Avoid generic one-use helpers,
legacy fallbacks, permissive coercion and new dependencies without need.

## Lifecycle

Keep `implementationStatus: "scaffold"` while required runtime behavior is
incomplete.

Change to `"ready"` when every runtime behavior in this prompt is implemented.

Tests are outside scope. Do not create/modify test files unless explicitly
requested.

If essential behavior is missing, keep `"scaffold"` and state what is missing.

